      "id": "action-observation-gap",
      "question": "What gaps remain in actions and observations?",
      "lead": "Generated action labels transfer effectively, while visual observations remain a major source of the sim–real gap.",
      "answer": "We disentangle actions and observations using four training sets on Task 1. R-25 covers the lower table region with 25 real demonstrations; S-25 covers the upper region with 25 simulation demonstrations. The animation below shows how the two mixed settings are constructed.",
      "analysis": "R-25 and S-25 both fail in the region absent from their training data. Mixing them expands coverage, but Mix-50 reaches only 2/5 and 4/5 success in the upper and lower regions. In Mix-50*, replacing the simulated images with real observations—while keeping the simulation action labels—raises both results to 5/5. This controlled comparison supports the transferability of generated actions and identifies visual alignment as a key remaining challenge. These results come from five real-world trials per region.",
