      "id": "sim-real-consistency",
      "question": "Can simulation reflect real-world performance?",
      "answer": "Both Task 1 policies achieve comparable success-rate levels across simulation and the real world: 31% versus 40% for real-data training, and 39% versus 35% for simulation-data training. This supports using the benchmark to evaluate humanoid policies. Establishing sim–real success-rate correlation is harder for humanoids than for fixed-base robot arms: whole-body pose, balance, and robot–object alignment make identical trial setups difficult to reproduce. Broader experiments across tasks and models are still needed to validate this correlation.",
